    {
      "text": "Stir together Worcestershire sauce, olive oil, garlic, hot sauce, and pepper in a large bowl. Add duck breasts; toss well to coat. Cover and marinate in the refrigerator, 30 minutes to overnight.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/hg8cdCRXqA0FkKsuWPIrJ3slHgY=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/114442-Grilled-Wild-Duck-Breast-DDMFS-4x3-step-3-11565-aab213c3e27041218f16a9929764a3a8.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/114442/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Preheat the grill for medium-high heat.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Remove duck from marinade and cook on the preheated grill to desired doneness, 5 to 7 minutes per side. An instant-read thermometer inserted into the center should read at least 165 degrees F (74 degrees C). Discard marinade.",
